    "summary": "High‑energy Vegas ’93 show – killer Help>Slip>Franklin’s & monster Other One",
    "review": "May 16, 1993 at the Sam Boyd Silver Bowl was a straight‑up fireworks display from the Dead. The first set is a quick warm‑up, but it’s the second set that really takes off – a smoking Help → Slip → Franklin’s that feels like a single, soaring groove, followed by a monster Other One that roars through the desert night. Highlights keep rolling: a ripping Wharf Rat climax, a juicy Cassidy jam, and an unstoppable Throwing Stones. Jerry is on fire all night – grin‑wide, 360° spin solos and a blistering Lovelight lead – while Phil’s bass twists and turns, anchoring those high‑octane peaks. Vince adds his trademark spacey textures (even if a few mixes push him forward), and despite Bob’s ragged vocal moments he still digs deep on rhythm guitar during the jams. The band stays locked in from Samson & Delilah all the way through a heartfelt Brokedown Palace encore, making this one of ’93’s most memorable Vegas outings.",
